assert kth_element([17, 24, 8, 23], 3) == 8
assert kth_element([16, 21, 25, 36, 4], 4) == 37
```

This function uses the Quickselect algorithm to efficiently find the kth smallest element in the array. The `quickselect` function partitions the array into elements less than the pivot, equal to the pivot, and greater than the pivot, and recursively selects the kth smallest element from the appropriate partition. This approach is more efficient than sorting the entire array, especially for large arrays.

